From b24b04f14e1af33d6153a6bb278c9d55940aec06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:38:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: the R47d 780M S-X8 mat-vec shape lookup as a
 device-probed default (R46b commit D)

R47d (lane-232) paired rows 1/2/4/8 against workgroups 64/128/256 over the four real 27B S-X8
decode shapes at n=1..8, two rounds each. The optimum is NOT one global pair: at n=1 the two FFN
orientations want rows=4/wg=256 while the 248320x5120 embed/output pair wants rows=8/wg=64, and
4096x14336 wants rows=1/wg=256. One pipeline-creation constant cannot express that, so this builds
one S-X8 f32 mat-vec pipeline per measured (rows, workgroup) variant per NUM_COLS and selects it at
dispatch from an exact (m, k, n) lookup - 31 cells, every one of them >= 0.97 of the probed default
in BOTH rounds. 17408x5120 at n=7 is absent on purpose: the sweep's winner there IS the default.

The rule ships only on the device class the sweep speaks for - subgroup width 64 with a 32 KiB
maxComputeSharedMemorySize, the SUBGROUP workgroup class, f32 activations - and only for those
exact cells. f16, q8_1 and the mat-vec-id path do NOT inherit an f32 timing result. Every
unmeasured shape, every n > 8 and every other device keep today's probed default, and a variant
whose own tmpsh[NUM_COLS][NUM_ROWS][BLOCK_SIZE] does not fit at its NUM_COLS is never built.
GGML_VK_SX8_MMV_ROWS / GGML_VK_SX8_MMV_WG still override, and setting either switches the lookup
off WHOLE for the run: a run that kept the measured table on the cells a sweep arm does not name
would be a mixed arm, and every receipt read off it would lie. A stderr receipt at pipeline
creation names the rule, ON or OFF, with the probed default and the device's own probe values.

STATED, because it is the acceptance surface: R47d measured lane-232's base, arifi/main 766cb9528,
which does not carry R46's n <= 3 whole-block decode. R46 replaces the decode math and the
row-blocking loop below n <= 3 and leaves the reduction shape untouched, so the shared-memory
arithmetic still holds - but the n=1/2/3 OPTIMA are UNVERIFIED on this kernel until they are
re-measured on the rebased stage. HQ owns that rerun.

Also fixes the R46 checker's F6: vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp claimed ANY workgroup size is correct for
mul_mat_vec_sx8.comp after R46. That is true only at NUM_COLS <= 3, where the whole-block path
runs; at NUM_COLS >= 4 the per-position kernel is kept verbatim and still derives its weight
position from tid & 31, so the multiple-of-32 invariant the host enforces is still load-bearing.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-types.h; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_585.py)
